## Validity & Staleness Rules

The agent must evaluate the staleness of any diary entry before using it as a cached answer.

### Staleness TTL Reference Table

| Category | Default TTL (steps) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `SYSTEM_CHECK` — disk space | 10 steps | Disk usage changes as files are written |
| `SYSTEM_CHECK` — memory | 5 steps | Memory is highly volatile |
| `SYSTEM_CHECK` — env vars | STABLE | Env vars don't change mid-session unless explicitly set |
| `DEPENDENCY_CHECK` | Until next install | Invalidated by any `INSTALL_ATTEMPT` entry |
| `INSTALL_ATTEMPT` (SUCCESS) | STABLE | A successful install does not need to be re-run |
| `INSTALL_ATTEMPT` (FAIL) | 1 step | Should be retried with a different strategy |
| `VERSION_FINDING` | STABLE | Runtime versions are fixed for the session |
| `COMMAND_OUTPUT` | 8 steps | General heuristic; adjust per command type |
| `PORT_CHECK` | 6 steps | Services can start/stop |
| `ERROR_ENCOUNTERED` | STABLE until resolved | Errors persist until a corrective action succeeds |
| `FILE_SIZE_CHECK` | Until file modification | Invalidated if the file is written to |
| `UPLOAD_CHECK` (SUCCESS) | STABLE | A completed upload is a permanent fact |
| `UPLOAD_CHECK` (FAIL) | 1 step | Retry after diagnosis |

### Staleness Evaluation Pseudocode

```
FUNCTION is_entry_valid(entry, current_step):
  IF entry.staleness_ttl == STABLE:
    RETURN TRUE

  IF entry.outcome_status == FAIL:
    RETURN FALSE  // FAIL entries are never used as a cache hit; they must be retried

  IF current_step > entry.valid_until_step:
    RETURN FALSE  // Entry has expired

  IF entry.category == DEPENDENCY_CHECK:
    IF any entry in diary WHERE category == INSTALL_ATTEMPT
       AND entry.timestamp > this_entry.timestamp:
      RETURN FALSE  // A later install invalidates dependency checks

  RETURN TRUE
```

