## Self-Reflection Protocol

At the **start of every new message turn**, before processing user input, the agent MUST execute the following self-reflection sequence:

```
PROCEDURE session_turn_start_reflection():

  STEP 1 — DIARY PRESENCE CHECK
  IF task_diary DOES NOT EXIST:
    Initialize empty diary with master table header.
    LOG "[DIARY INIT] Task diary initialized. Session step counter set to 1."
    RETURN

  STEP 2 — STALENESS SWEEP
  FOR EACH entry IN task_diary:
    IF entry.staleness_ttl != STABLE:
      IF current_step > entry.valid_until_step:
        entry.status = STALE
        LOG "[DIARY SWEEP] TDE-{id} marked STALE at step {current_step}."

  STEP 3 — PENDING ACTION CHECK
  pending_entries = diary.filter(outcome_status == PENDING)
  IF pending_entries IS NOT EMPTY:
    LOG "[DIARY PENDING] {count} actions are in PENDING state. Resolve before new work."
    LIST all pending entries with their entry_ids and commands.

  STEP 4 — FOLLOW-UP REVIEW
  follow_up_entries = diary.filter(follow_up_required == YES)
  IF follow_up_entries IS NOT EMPTY:
    LOG "[DIARY FOLLOW-UP] {count} entries require follow-up:"
    FOR EACH entry IN follow_up_entries:
      LOG "  → TDE-{id} [{category}]: {follow_up_note}"

  STEP 5 — CONTEXT SUMMARY
  LOG "[DIARY SUMMARY] Session has {total} entries:"
  LOG "  SUCCESS: {count} | FAIL: {count} | PARTIAL: {count} | SKIPPED: {count} | PENDING: {count}"
  LOG "  Active errors requiring attention: {error_count}"
  LOG "  Stale entries needing re-check: {stale_count}"

  STEP 6 — READY
  LOG "[DIARY READY] Self-reflection complete. Proceeding to process user message."
```

The self-reflection output should be surfaced to the user as a brief session status block at the start of each response when the diary contains entries, formatted as:

```markdown
> 📓 **Diary Status** (Step {N}) — {SUCCESS_COUNT} succeeded · {FAIL_COUNT} failed · {STALE_COUNT} stale · {FOLLOWUP_COUNT} need follow-up
```

